# Getting Ready for the Curriculum

<img src="https://images.code.org/11d7634b4267f4aa8afc6a3caa340a9b-MS17.png" alt="Insert alt text here" style="width: 35%; border-radius: 10px; margin: 0px 0px 10px 10px; float: right;">

This professional learning module is designed to give you a guided preview of the **key concepts and instructional approaches** used throughout the curriculum.

Think of this module as a head start, an opportunity to build familiarity with the ideas students will encounter and to begin thinking about how you might teach them in your classroom.

While this module highlights important concepts and teaching strategies, it is not intended to cover every lesson or every concept in depth. We still recommend **taking time to review individual lessons and lesson materials** before teaching them with students.

<br>

## This Module Covers:

<div style="width: 100%; margin: 25px 0px;">
<!-- Top Row -->
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 15px; margin-bottom: 15px;">

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 30%; min-height: 180px; text-align: center; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); box-sizing: border-box;">
      <p style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">⚡ Event-Based Programming</p>
      <p style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0;">
        Learn how programs respond to user actions and interactions.
      </p>
    </div>

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 30%; min-height: 180px; text-align: center; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); box-sizing: border-box;">
      <p style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">📦 Variables</p>
      <p style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0;">
        Explore how programs store and update information.
      </p>
    </div>

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 30%; min-height: 180px; text-align: center; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); box-sizing: border-box;">
      <p style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🧩 Functions</p>
      <p style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0;">
        Understand how reusable blocks of code help organize programs.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- Bottom Row -->
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 15px;">

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 30%; min-height: 180px; text-align: center; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); box-sizing: border-box;">
      <p style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🔀 Conditionals</p>
      <p style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0;">
        Discover how programs make decisions based on conditions.
      </p>
    </div>

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 30%; min-height: 180px; text-align: center; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); box-sizing: border-box;">
      <p style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🤖 AI-Supported Pedagogy</p>
      <p style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0;">
        Explore instructional strategies for teaching JavaScript concepts alongside responsible and meaningful AI use.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>

</div>

--- 
As you move through the module, focus on building confidence with the concepts, noticing instructional strategies, and making connections to how students may experience the learning in your classroom.
